'''Pantora''' was the primary [[moon]] in [[orbit]] around the [[planet]] [[Orto Plutonia]],<ref name="Dark Disciple" /> in the [[Pantora system]], located in the [[Sujimis sector]] of the [[Outer Rim Territories]],<ref name="Heir" /> in grid square P-19 on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]].<ref name="Coordinates" /> It was the [[homeworld]] of the [[Pantoran]]s, who were led by the [[Pantoran Assembly]]<ref name="Trespass" /> and the [[Supreme Chairman]] of Pantora, a post held by [[Chi Cho]], who was later replaced by [[Baron]] [[Notluwiski Papanoida]]. Pantora was a member of the [[Galactic Republic]] and therefore represented in the [[Galactic Senate]]. During the [[Clone Wars]], Pantora remained loyal to the Republic and [[Riyo Chuchi]] served as its [[senator]].<ref name="DBPantora" />

==History==
Pantora held a claim to sovereignty over the [[planet]] it orbited by dint of being the only inhabited body in its system, though they were unaware that [[Orto Plutonia]] was in fact inhabited by a [[Sentience|sentient]], if primitive, species known as the [[Talz]].<ref name="Trespass" /> One [[Unidentified Pantoran baron|baron]] from Pantora was selected by the [[Adrialla's mother|Queen]] of [[Eiram]] for her daughter, [[Princess]] [[Adrialla]], to [[Marriage|marry]] because of the usefulness of such an alliance. The baron had a specific hope of beginning [[fuel]] [[mining]] within Eiram's oceans. However, Adrialla had already found love with her future wife [[Odelia]].<ref name="Convergence">''[[The High Republic: Convergence]]''</ref>

During the [[Clone Wars]], a [[Glid Station|Republic outpost]] was established on Orto Plutonia at the request of [[Chairman]] [[Chi Cho]], who feared that Pantora might be targeted by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatists]] due to its [[Galactic Republic|Republic]] leanings. The outpost, as well as a [[droid]] base that had indeed been established there as well, ran afoul of the Talz and all personnel were [[Skirmish on Orto Plutonia|wiped out]]. This led to the discovery of the Talz by a joint Pantoran-Republic task force sent to investigate the loss of contact, placing Pantora's claim to the planet into question. Chairman Cho refused to either acknowledge the Talz's sentience or renounce Pantora's claim and deliberately aggrandized the situation into spawning a brief but bloody [[One-Day War|conflict]] for control, losing his life in the process. The [[Pantoran Assembly]], having learned of Chairman Cho's actions, declared him out of order and had [[Senator]] [[Riyo Chuchi]] renounce their claim in favor of acknowledging the Talz's sovereignty over their [[homeworld]], forging peace between the [[Pantoran]]s and the Talz.<ref name="Trespass" />

Pantora was later [[Blockade of Pantora|blockaded]] by the [[Trade Federation]], who falsely claimed that the [[moon]] owed them outstanding debts but in reality, were hoping to pressure the Pantorans into joining the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]]. Senator Chuchi fiercely defended her world in the [[Galactic Senate|Senate]] and begged for a resolution in Pantora's favor, but widespread anti-Republic sentiment grew as the Senate appeared slow to act and unsympathetic to their plight. The situation escalated when Chairman [[Notluwiski Papanoida |Papanoida's]] [[Gender|daughters]] were [[Kidnapping of the Papanoida daughter|kidnapped]] by [[bounty hunter]]s hired by the Federation to put additional pressure on them, but a joint investigation by the Pantoran officials and [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] [[Ahsoka Tano]] uncovered the truth and the Federation was forced to remove its [[blockade]] in order to save face.<ref name="Sphere of Influence" />

Shortly after the [[Proclamation of the New Order|rise]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], [[Clone Force 99]] stopped at a spaceport in Pantora to refuel, scramble [[Marauder (Omicron-class)|their ship's]] signature, and pick up supplies. As [[Hunter]], [[Echo]], and [[Omega]] wandered through the marketplace of the planet, they saw civilians celebrating the end of the [[Clone Wars]]. As Hunter sold Echo who was disguised as a droid in order to get [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]], Omega encountered bounty hunter [[Fennec Shand]] who gained the girl's trust. However, Hunter realized the threat Shand possessed, leading a chase between the bounty hunter and the clones before Clone Force 99 managed to escape from Pantora.<ref name="Cornered" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Dialogue|Tech|By my calculations, the closest planet is&hellip;Pantora.|Hunter|Well, Pantora it is.|Omega|Pantora it is.|attr=[[Tech]], Hunter, and Omega erroneously referring to Pantora as a planet|src=<ref name="Cornered" />}}
Pantora was first mentioned in the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' episode "[[Trespass]],"<ref name="Trespass" /> and first appeared in the episode "[[Sphere of Influence]]."<ref name="Sphere of Influence" />

Although Pantora is a moon, it has been referred to as a planet frequently: the [[Pantoran Assembly Representative]] refers to it as a "sovereign planet" in "Trespass";<ref name="Trespass" /> it is also called a planet in "Sphere of Influence"<ref name="Sphere of Influence" /> and "[[Cornered]]."<ref name="Cornered" /> In the initial hardcover and [[The High Republic: The Eye of Darkness (audiobook)|audiobook]] release of ''[[The High Republic: The Eye of Darkness]]'', the list of planets brought under Nihil control by the [[expansion of the Stormwall]] includes Pantora. Given that Pantora was already within the [[Occlusion Zone]], the digital release edits the list and instead places [[Abtin]] behind the new Stormwall border.<ref name="Post-release edit">{{WordPress|subdomain=numidianprime|url=2023/11/16/the-occlusion-zone-of-the-nihil-2|name=Numidian Prime|text=The Occlusion Zone of the Nihil|archivedate=20231201060644}}</ref>

